task: bench-refresh
agent: opus5-bench
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/bench-refresh
worktree: ../okay-wt-bench

why: the operator asked for the comparison benchmarks to be re-run and
  every number in the documentation refreshed. docs/benchmarks.md's own
  rule is that lanes quoted together were measured in the same session;
  its tables have accumulated across a dozen sessions on hosts of
  varying quiet. One session, one host, one protocol makes the tables
  comparable to each other again.

what: re-measure every CROSS-LIBRARY lane (the ones that quote
  cats-effect / ZIO / kyo / fs2 / atnos / circe) — CompareBenchmark,
  DirectBenchmark, Reader, Writer, Choice, Async, StreamOps, Merge,
  ChunkFlush, IdiomaticApi, Resource, Generator, Text, Codec, Rag, and
  FairnessProbe's floor lanes — in one session on the freshly-booted
  quiet box, append every row to src/jmh/history.tsv, and write the new
  numbers into docs/benchmarks.md sections 0-11 with the run's date and
  protocol stated. Scope chosen by the operator over "everything in
  compare/" and over "headline only".

predict: most rows land within noise of the current table. The box is
  quiet and freshly booted where several of the standing rows were
  measured "box shared with sibling builds all day", so the honest
  expectation is that MANY rows move DOWN together — which is a host
  effect, not a win, and the doc must say so rather than claim
  improvement. Orderings between libraries should not change; if one
  does, that row gets re-run before it is written.

CAUTION — MACHINE STATE THIS CLAIM OWNS:
  both scalascript launchd guards are UNLOADED for the duration
  (operator's decision, 2026-09-07):
    launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/io.scalascript.build-ram-guard.plist
    launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/io.scalascript.kill-stale-builders.plist
  If this session dies, whoever finds this claim must load them back.
